WEBVTT

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.680
<i>They disappeared?</i>

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.110
Too bad! That was a feint!

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.480
We need to regroup.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.040
She'll beat us here.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.430
You won't get away, young man.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.430
The lovey-dovey couple with the chains
 got away last time though.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.500
Hayate!

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.680
That was because she shielded Break Chain,

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.990
and you hesitated to hit her.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.940
We could've won that fight.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.450
Sorry.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.450
I see.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:06.620
He can stop us from using our 
Dagger and Blade, huh?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.840
You can use these obstacles 
to stop our forward mobility.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.360
Smart thinking.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:07.040
But Dagger and Blade aren't 
that easy to beat, young man!

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.030
Too bad, young man, Koyori-chan.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.470
These are hunting grounds.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.980
It's time to end this.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:28.700
I can't use my sword.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.640
I'll use a shield!

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.150
Why are you doing this?

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.840
Why?

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.650
Because we're Hand Shakers, young man.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.400
We don't want to fight!

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:45.740
I'll give you a different reason then.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.880
Because we have a wish.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.410
That's why we fight, 
and that's why we'll beat you!

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.420
You don't even know if 
your wish will come true.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.440
It might.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.100
That's good enough.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.420
I'll steel my resolve...

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.110
and fight!

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.070
I guess we have to do it...

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.760
Don't worry.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:09.830
I've got a plan.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.890
<i>They're too fast for us to escape.</i>

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.180
<i>But there has to be some 
way for things to mesh.</i>

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.580
<i>If I lose, Koyori will...</i>

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:24.940
<i>I'll protect Koyori!</i>

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.120
A smokescreen!

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.160
That's clever.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.830
Not bad, young man.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.080
But even if you run, 
my clone will be waiting for you!

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.050
<i>Damn it? Another clone?</i>

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:44.880
He's really good...

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.960
But I won't let you get away!

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:48.830
<i>This is amazing.</i>

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.810
<i>My body's responding on its own.</i>

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.530
<i>I've only fought once before,</i>

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.670
<i>but I know what they're going to do.</i>

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.140
<i>I can use my gears freely.</i>

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:02.360
<i>Does that mean my level as 
a Hand Shaker has gone up?</i>

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.920
Sorry for letting go!

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.560
<i>Koyori...</i>

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.700
<i>I can protect her forever like this.</i>

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:14.540
<i>That's right.</i>

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.310
<i>I swore that I wouldn't let go.</i>

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.710
<i>That I'd never let go of her hand!</i>

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:23.960
This way!

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.240
<i>Just a little more...</i>

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.360
<i>A little more!</i>

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.860
I won't let you escape!

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.530
<i>Are they following us?</i>

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.320
<i>If we make it up here...</i>

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.260
Let's go, Koyori!

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.300
Looks like you've chosen to fight.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:10.740
Let's finish this, Hayate.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:14.310
I'll follow you anywhere, Senpai.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.070
You're mine, young man!

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.570
<i>I can't tell which are the clones, but...</i>

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.080
<i>Up here...</i>

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:40.730
They meshed.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.370
He could tell which one was me?

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.350
No...

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:55.850
He lured us up here?

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.360
You can't surround me up here!

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.360
What are you doing?

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:12.950
Come on, Tazuna-kun!

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:14.070
Right!

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.340
Hayate!

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.890
Azuma-san!

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.920
Let's finish this as men!

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.920
Hayate!

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:42.870
Hayate...

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:46.690
I'm sorry...

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:53.800
Chizuru-san.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.680
You won.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.340
That's how this battle works.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:10.490
You did well, my subordinate.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:14.060
Thank you.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.680
I'm really sorry!

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.010
I'm sorry!

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:29.790
S-Stop it...

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.990
That's what Hand Shakers are supposed to do.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:34.030
Even if we didn't know,

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.920
we said all kinds of really selfish things...

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.720
We have to apologize.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:38.800
That's right.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.760
If she doesn't charge, 
and loses her power, she dies?

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:45.000
If she loses, she dies? That's crazy!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.750
I'm sorry I'm so healthy.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.740
I told her not to just let him 
protect her, to fight for herself...

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:55.880
Without even knowing what was going on...

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.140
I'm terrible.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.010
I'm sorry, Koyori-chan.

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.550
Koyori-chan.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.220
Thank you.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:11.520
You're very nice.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:14.620
But you're treating me 
like a kid. Please stop.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:24.560
Anyway, is it because of how her body works

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.170
that Koyori-chan doesn't have a Nimrod?

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:31.230
I have theories, but haven't 
been able to prove them yet.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.660
That's about where we are.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.170
I need more data!

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.160
Want some shumai?

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:44.680
I recommend it.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.690
Sure!

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:49.690
It's good!

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:54.220
I'm glad that Koyori-kun's safe, though,

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.200
and that we didn't end up enemies.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.870
It was a fair fight.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:03.160
I won't lie and say I'm not upset, 
but I'm not going to hate you for it.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.130
Right, Hayate?

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.200
Yeah.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.330
Chizuru-san...

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.210
Hayate-san...

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:11.130
More importantly,

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:14.540
you fought and protected Koyori-chan, 
who doesn't have a Nimrod,

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:16.160
and you beat us.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:20.630
Koyori-chan, this young man is a great guy.

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:26.500
Don't let the younger kid 
beat you, my subordinate!

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.830
I'm really sorry he got me.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:36.090
By the way, what's your name?

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.550
Name?

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:40.360
Yeah.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:45.840
Remember how we called ourselves 
Dagger Shadow and Blade Shadow?

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:48.230
You've got something like that, right?

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.450
Oh, right. That.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:02.670
I kept meaning to bring it up...

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:03.820
Um, you know...

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.500
It happens, right?

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:06.640
Wait!

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:09.850
You're like their guardian.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:13.640
You're the one who told them 
about the Hand Shakers, right?

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.100
Jeez!

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:18.160
Oh, I remembered.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:21.070
But you know, when you're over 30...

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:23.530
Don't use your age as an excuse.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:26.810
It's rude to people who are 
the same age and are working hard.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:27.540
O-Okay...

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:32.040
And if girls use their age as an 
excuse, they get old real fast!

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.500
I just forgot to say it...

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:37.610
It's fine! You don't look old at all.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:37.610
Right, right, right.

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:39.050
You look like a middle-school student.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.320
Who are you calling a middle-school student?

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:42.040
Jeez!

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.050
Learn your lesson!

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:46.430
Makihara-san, you learn
your lesson right now!

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.910
Understand why I'm getting mad at you

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.720
and learn your lesson,

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:53.260
or you won't grow!

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:54.330
Right...

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:58.510
And I'm going to get really 
mad at you later, Hayate!

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:01.830
If you pay for the next drinking 
party I'll let you off.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:05.320
That's a surprisingly solid threat.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.860
How long are you going to keep holding me?

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:10.060
Jeez!

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:13.830
Sorry, you're so light.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.570
I do not have the body of an 
elementary-school student!

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:18.520
It's closer to a middle-school student!

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:20.170
I didn't say that, but sorry.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.340
Shut up.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:27.130
It looks like you haven't heard

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:30.350
that holding hands is 
directly linked to fighting.

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:33.940
You mean it'll make it 
obvious we're Hand Shakers?

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.350
That's part of it.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:39.740
First, when two Hand Shakers hold hands,

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.360
they exchange memories and emotions, right?

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.640
You know, when you hold their hand,

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:51.870
you can kind of tell what they're 
thinking or feeling, right?

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:56.620
No, not in Koyori-kun's case.

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:57.880
I see.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:01.240
She was asleep the whole time...

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:04.060
That's why I didn't feel anything.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.100
I see.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:18.280
If you have something you want to hide, 
you can hide it by focusing on it.

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.640
And of course, because it's only for 
stuff on the surface of your mind,

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.620
it's not a perfect synchronization.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:25.110
Are you hiding something?

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.740
I'll get back to the point.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.540
I was thinking about 
something more fundamental.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:32.330
Senpai!

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:36.120
Do you know what the trigger 
for entering the Ziggurat is?

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:38.240
No...

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:41.130
So far it's just been like 
we're being caught up in it.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:46.580
One way is when two sets of Hand Shakers 
holding hands get within a certain distance.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:49.640
Then it's automatic.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.920
The data indicates the range 
is about a kilometer.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.480
There've been cases where multiple 
groups have been caught up at once.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:10.000
The other is when a pair of 
Hand Shakers holding hands

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.160
focus on a target and 
challenge them to battle.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:17.690
In other words, once someone 
knows you're a Hand Shaker,

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:21.170
you can be challenged, even 
if you're not holding hands.

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:26.260
This is another thing you can do if the 
target's within a range of one kilometer.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.450
There's also data that shows if 
you get over a kilometer away

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:33.180
from the enemy you'll be 
knocked out of the Ziggurat.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.300
Th-Then...

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:43.530
I'm basically holding a sign saying, 
"I'm a Hand Shaker" as I walk?

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:51.700
Well, it's also possible to assume 
you're just a lovey-dovey couple.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.160
Sorry.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.120
I forgot about that stuff.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:02.110
But I figured you'd be able to tell somehow.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.630
You're not a very reliable backer.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:10.120
Normally, you try not to stand out so 
as not to get challenged to battles,

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:12.350
and you hide your name when you fight.

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:14.970
Otherwise, you'll have to bring the fight

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:17.640
into the real world, 
and your daily life, right?

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:19.640
Oh, jeez!

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:23.280
Fine, Hayate and I will be your guardians,

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:25.650
since you can actually count on us!

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:28.460
You can count on me?

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:31.660
I will be a guardian you can count on.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.660
Senpai...

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:38.090
Guardians? But...

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:40.700
Does it bother you that you beat us?

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:45.080
That's because we're weaker than you.

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:48.170
We just weren't strong enough.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:52.410
There's no need for it 
to bother you, or Koyori-chan.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:58.650
You beat us, so I don't want you losing

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:00.550
because of this careless guardian!

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:06.940
We've only been in two battles though.

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:10.380
Chizuru-san, Hayate-san...

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.110
Thank you.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:21.260
Isn't that nice, Tazuna-kun, Koyori-kun?

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:22.960
I'm feeling relieved, too.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:32.600
Are you an angel?

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:40.970
Okay, so here's our first piece of advice.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:42.570
Okay!

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:44.080
Single Gear.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:44.940
How about it?

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.440
Jeez...

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.800
Your name!

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.880
Your Hand Shaker name.

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:55.470
I just told you that using your 
real name's dangerous, right?

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.260
So I thought of one.

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:59.490
Normally you fight together as pair,

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:03.500
but you fought to protect 
Koyori-chan all by yourself.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.960
Your Nimrod is a gear.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.000
So that's why it's Single Gear.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.370
That's right, but don't explain it!

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:14.320
I'm so embarrassed, I'm going to explode!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.590
That wasn't a compliment!

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:19.350
Single Gear...

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.670
Thank you.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:28.810
It's okay.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.480
You can rely on us.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:31.270
Okay!

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:01.330
They were strong, huh?

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.790
Yup.

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:05.770
Tazuna-kun was really tough.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.900
I told them I didn't feel 
bitter because we lost, right?

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:17.500
That's a lie...

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.570
I thought so.

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:23.880
I'm really frustrated!

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.740
I was sure that we...

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:29.760
that you and I could beat anyone!

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.850
That we could do anything!

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:34.120
I hope they both explode.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:42.890
Chizuru-san...

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.530
Thank you.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:53.380
Sorry I'm such a worthless boss.

00:18:57.010 --> 00:19:04.620
To be honest, you really help me out a lot.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:08.810
I guess you really are a guy...

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:17.460
I'm... I'm really upset, too...

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:18.380
Hayate! K-Keep your eyes on the road!

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:22.470
I'm sorry, I can't see what's in front 
of me because of the sweat in my heart!

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.970
Oh, no! You idiot!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.200
We're going to die! We're going to die!

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:29.870
We're going to die!

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:33.260
You idiot! Stupid Hayate!

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:36.000
I thought we were going to die.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.230
I'm really sorry.

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:43.820
As long as you understand.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:46.840
But you know,

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:50.280
we lost, and it's frustrating...

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:54.010
But those little kids are risking 
their lives and working really hard.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:57.250
I think we, their elders, 
need to work even harder.

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:00.760
You and I can do anything together.

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:04.330
Even if our fight's over, 
I still think that's true.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:06.240
That's right.

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.450
I'll do my best, too!

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:09.100
We can do anything!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.770
Okay, let's go drinking.

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:12.720
You're paying.

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:14.350
Tomorrow we've got work,

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:15.770
but we can do anything.

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:18.760
I'll go with you, Senpai!

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:21.360
Today I'll actually use my credit card!

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:24.280
Go easy on me!

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:29.180
By the way, weren't you saying 
something in the car, Senpai?

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:31.580
Something about me helping you out?

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:33.230
Are you bringing that up now?

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.450
You really are...

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:37.290
Senpai, that hurts.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.800
Let's just go.

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.160
Here?

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:42.110
Here, right?

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:43.710
I'm getting the best stuff they have tonight.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:45.460
It's expensive!

00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:13.740
<i>A brief period of peace visits them.</i>

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:15.900
<i>What they see, what they hear,
 what they touch...</i>

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:17.870
<i>The warmth they feel from the heart.</i>

00:23:18.420 --> 00:23:21.580
<i>Uncertainty, impatience, and loneliness.</i>

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:24.340
<i>A freezing heartbeat felt from the heart.</i>

00:23:24.640 --> 00:23:26.250
<i>The trump card is the siblings.</i>

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:27.510
<i>He is the Joker.</i>

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:32.700
<i>Next time, Hand Shakers Episode 5: Meet Yet.</i>

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:36.390
<i>The man who stands in the path of their run</i>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:38.430
<i>drives a stake into the young man's heart.</i>
